# Task 156-008 Plan: Brain Self-Rebuild Gate

## Approach
Add a pre-flight build-staleness check that runs at the start of sprint planning.
Compare `dist/orchestra/sprint-phases.js` mtime against `.deckent/sprint-state.json` mtime.
If dist is newer than sprint-state → emit SPRINT→USER:BUILD_STALE_WARNING event.
NO build invocation; pure mtime read + event emit + fail-safe.

## Files to Modify
1. `src/orchestra/sprint-phases.ts`
   - Add `statSync` to node:fs imports
   - Add new exported function `checkBuildStaleness(projectRoot, sprintId)`
   - Call from start of `runPlanPhase` (before any state mutation)
   - Function returns boolean (true = warning emitted)
   - Fail-safe: any I/O error → debugLog only, no throw

2. `tests/orchestra/brain-rebuild-gate.test.ts` (new)
   - Mock node:fs (statSync, existsSync)
   - Mock event-stream (writeEvent)
   - Test cases:
     a. dist 1h newer than sprint-state → warning emitted with correct payload
     b. dist older than sprint-state → no warning
     c. dist file missing → no warning, no crash
     d. sprint-state file missing → no warning, no crash
     e. statSync throws → no warning, no crash (fail-safe)
     f. equal mtimes → no warning (strict greater-than)

## Expected Channel
`SPRINT→USER:BUILD_STALE_WARNING`
Source: 'sprint', Target: 'user'
Payload: { distMtime: ISO string, sprintStateMtime: ISO string, ageSeconds: number }

## Constraints
- ADR-008: Brain modules only — no circular imports
- ADR-024: Live inside sprint-phases.ts (extracted from sprint-controller)
- NO `npm run build` or any build invocation
- NO global tsc/vitest invocation — only `npx vitest run path/to/this.test.ts`
